{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792666356,"nonce":"7ywnULYVq30S6l2drrwDne69ktk=","title":"LSP re-analyses an open page after a server restart although its BLADE editor index is valid","message":"A requests sent right after didOpen on a fresh server was never answered from the persisted .bidx. The front thread's cache is not configured until the worker finishes initialize, so the first request missed it and was forwarded; the worker then saw no live analysis and ran a full one. analyze_document already published the index's diagnostics, but deferred requests still triggered analysis.\n\nReproducer: RayDE workspace, `rayzor lsp`, didOpen src/rayde/ui/Welcome.hx then hover at once, restart and repeat. Hover took about 7s on every restart; the saved index loaded (same input hash, complete, dependencies current) and was ignored. Busy-machine observation, not an isolated benchmark.\n\nFix: the worker answers a deferred request from the editor index before it starts a full analysis. Hover after restart: 7.1s -\u003e 0.16s with no checking cycle.\n\nStill open: the cache key hashes every file on every class path and the stdlib, so editing any one file invalidates every page's index; WorkspaceIndex::start re-parses all .hx files on each start and persists nothing.","files":null}]}